There is a missing step in your instructions, and there were also some missing files 
in the repository, which should now be fixed.

So if you try again with :

$ git clone https://github.com/juba/scatterD3
$ cd scatterD3
$ npm install
$ LC_ALL=C R --no-save <<EOT
> install.packages("packer")
> packer::bundle_prod()
> EOT

I think it should work. You would need a working installation of nodejs and npm on 
your machine though, to be able to run the `npm install` command that will download 
the npm dependencies in a node_modules folder.

Let me know if you encounter any other problems.

Thanks again,

Julien

